  pages     = "97--111",
  abstract  = "There are two popular statistical models for meta-analysis, the
               fixed-effect model and the random-effects model. The fact that
               these two models employ similar sets of formulas to compute
               statistics, and sometimes yield similar estimates for the various
               parameters, may lead people to believe that the models are
