  pages     = "e2436",
  abstract  = "A common feature in cohort studies is when there is a baseline
               measurement of the continuous follow-up or outcome variable.
               Common examples include baseline measurements of physiological
               characteristics such as blood pressure or heart rate in studies
               where the outcome is post-baseline measurement of the same
