              an early elective cesarean section to avoid greater complications
              from possible later non-elective operative delivery. A basic risk
              prediction model for later non-elective operative delivery
              involves only antepartum markers. Because adding intrapartum
              markers to this risk prediction model increases AUC by 0.02, we
              questioned whether this small improvement is worthwhile. A key
              decision-analytic quantity is the risk threshold, here the risk of
              later non-elective operative delivery at which a patient would be
              indifferent between an early elective cesarean section and usual
