              order to make informed inferences about that intervention. Random
              effects allow the target population outcomes to vary among trials.
              Since meta-analysis is often an important element in helping shape
              public health policy, society depends on biostatisticians to help
              ensure that the methodology is sound. Yet when meta-analysis
              involves randomized binomial trials with low event rates, the
