  journal   = "Stat. Med.",
  publisher = "Wiley",
  volume    =  45,
  number    = "6-7",
  pages     = "e70449",
  abstract  = "The adoption of complex innovative clinical trial designs has
               steadily increased in recent years. These are trial designs that
               have one or more unconventional features-often resulting in
               multiple stages-with the goal of improving on conventional
               single-stage, fixed-setting designs in terms of efficiency, for
               example, by reducing the required sample size or the time to
               establish findings about an intervention. The motivation for
               these designs may not be difficult to follow, but their set-up
