              randomization test via Monte Carlo simulation, developing an
              efficient algorithm that makes multiple comparisons possible that
              would not be possible using a standard algorithm, demonstrate the
              preservation of type I error rate, and explore the relationship of
              statistical power to the randomization procedure in the presence
              of a time trend and outliers. We distinguish between the
              interpretation of the p-value in the randomization test and in the
