  journal  = "Stat. Med.",
  volume   =  41,
  number   =  2,
  pages    = "242--257",
  abstract = "A variety of methods have been proposed to estimate a standard
              deviation, when only a sample range has been observed or reported.
              This problem occurs in the interpretation of individual clinical
              studies that are incompletely reported, and also in their
              incorporation into meta-analyses. The methods differ with respect
              to their focus being either on the standard deviation in the
