  journal  = "Stat. Med.",
  abstract = "Previous articles in Statistics in Medicine describe how to
              calculate the sample size required for external validation of
              prediction models with continuous and binary outcomes. The minimum
              sample size criteria aim to ensure precise estimation of key
              measures of a model's predictive performance, including measures
              of calibration, discrimination, and net benefit. Here, we extend
