              confidence interval width for the calibration slope measuring the
              agreement between predicted risks (from the model) and observed
              risks (derived using pseudo-observations to account for censoring)
              on the log cumulative hazard scale. Precise estimation of
              calibration curves, discrimination, and net-benefit can also be
              checked in this framework. The process requires assumptions about
              the validation population in terms of the (i) distribution of the
              model's linear predictor and (ii) event and censoring
