  volume    =  17,
  number    =  3,
  pages     = "e70042",
  abstract  = "ABSTRACT In regression analysis, associations between continuous
               predictors and the outcome are often assumed to be linear.
               However, modeling the associations as non‐linear can improve
               model fit. Many flexible modeling techniques, like (fractional)
               polynomials and spline‐based approaches, are available. Such
               methods can be systematically compared in simulation studies,
               which require suitable performance measures to evaluate the
               accuracy of the estimated curves against the true data‐generating
               functions. Although various measures have been proposed in the
               literature, no systematic overview exists so far. To fill this
               gap, we introduce a categorization of performance measures for
