  number    =  3,
  pages     = "175--183",
  abstract  = "Abstract Purpose of Review The evidence regarding the clinical
               effects of drug-drug interactions (DDIs) is scarce and limited.
               Pharmacoepidemiologic studies could help fill in this important
               knowledge gap. Here, we review the pharmacoepidemiology of DDIs
               with a focus on cohort designs. We also highlight the
               decision-making process with respect to different aspects of
               cohort study design, potential biases that may arise during this
               decision process, and mitigation strategies. Recent Findings
               Considering the pharmacologic mechanism of the DDI of interest as
