              for interpreters had prevented them from offering a study to
              potential candidates (mean, 3.2; SD = 1.2). Non-Caucasian
              respondents were more likely to agree that ``fear of unknown side
              effects'' was a deterrent for minorities (p < 0.01), ``minorities
