  journal  = "Lancet Infect. Dis.",
  volume   =  20,
  number   =  10,
  pages    = "e251--e260",
  abstract = "The term metagenomics refers to the use of sequencing methods to
              simultaneously identify genomic material from all organisms
              present in a sample, with the advantage of greater taxonomic
              resolution than culture or other methods. Applications include
              pathogen detection and discovery, species characterisation,
              antimicrobial resistance detection, virulence profiling, and study
              of the microbiome and microecological factors affecting health.
              However, metagenomics involves complex and multistep processes and
              there are important technical and methodological challenges that
              require careful consideration to support valid inference. We
              co-ordinated a multidisciplinary, international expert group to
              establish reporting guidelines that address specimen processing,
              nucleic acid extraction, sequencing platforms, bioinformatics
              considerations, quality assurance, limits of detection, power and
