  volume   =  29,
  pages    =  100368,
  abstract = "Approximate Bayesian Computation (ABC) techniques are a suite of
              model fitting methods which can be implemented without a using
              likelihood function. In order to use ABC in a time-efficient
              manner users must make several design decisions including how to
              code the ABC algorithm and the type of ABC algorithm to use.
              Furthermore, ABC relies on a number of user defined choices which
