              of STARE-HI principles to be addressed in papers describing
              evaluations of Health Informatics interventions is presented.
              These principles include formulation of title and abstract, of
              introduction (e.g. scientific background, study objectives), study
              context (e.g. organizational setting, system details), methods
              (e.g. study design, outcome measures), results (e.g. study
              findings, unexpected observations) and discussion and conclusion
              of an IT evaluation paper. CONCLUSION: A comprehensive list of
              principles relevant for properly describing Health Informatics
              evaluations has been developed. When manuscripts submitted to
              Health Informatics journals and general medical journals adhere to
