  pages    = "124--131",
  abstract = "OBJECTIVES: To provide GRADE guidance on how to prepare Summary of
              Findings tables and Evidence Profiles for time-to-event outcomes
              with a focus on the calculation of the corresponding absolute
              effect estimates. STUDY DESIGN AND SETTING: This guidance was
              justified by a research project identifying frequent errors and
              limitations in the presentation of time-to-event outcomes in the
              Summary of Findings tables. We developed this guidance through an
              iterative process that included membership consultation, feedback,
              presentation, and discussion at meetings of the GRADE Working
              Group. RESULTS: Review authors need to carefully consider the
              definition of the outcome of interest; although often the event is
              used as label for the outcome of interest (e.g., death or
