              29 studies: seven proposed approaches for prioritization and 25
              conducted prioritization exercises (three studies did both). The
              included studies addressed the following fields: clinical (n = 19;
              66\%), public health (n = 10; 34\%), and health policy and systems
              (n = 8; 28\%), with six studies (21\%) addressing more than one
