              relationships. Funding agencies have called for all health
              researchers to incorporate sex and gender into their studies;
              however, the way forward has been unclear to many, particularly
              due to the varied definition of gender. We argue that just as
              there is no standardized definition of gender, there can be no
              standardized measurement thereof. However, numerous measurable
              gender-related variables may influence individual or
