               invited 47 members of the ISPOR Digital Health Special Interest
               Group, 18 of whom became the Delphi panel. The first, second, and
               third survey rounds were completed by 18, 11, and 10 respondents,
               respectively. After consolidating results, the PICOTS-ComTeC
               acronym emerged, involving 9 domains (population, intervention,
               comparator, outcome, timing, setting, communication, technology,
               and context) and 32 optional subcategories. CONCLUSIONS:
