  journal   = "Ann. Thorac. Surg.",
  publisher = "Elsevier BV",
  volume    =  72,
  number    =  2,
  pages     = "323--326",
  abstract  = "Receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve analysis is a
               useful method to measure the ability of a clinical risk model to
               discriminate between hospital deaths and survivors. Its use in
               medicine originated as a method for synthesizing the specificity
               and sensitivity of diagnostic tests across a spectrum of possible
               cut points. The area under the ROC curve can be interpreted as a
