  abstract  = "Systematic reviews and meta-analyses are increasingly popular
               study designs in clinical research. A systematic review is a
               summary of the medical literature that uses explicit and
               reproducible methods for searching the literature and critical
               appraisal of individual studies; in contrast, a meta-analysis is
               a mathematical synthesis of the results of these individual
               studies. These study designs can be useful tools for summarizing
