  pages    = "1397--1403",
  abstract = "The area under the receiver operating characteristic (ROC) curve
              (AUC) is commonly used for assessing the discriminative ability of
              prediction models even though the measure is criticized for being
              clinically irrelevant and lacking an intuitive interpretation.
              Every tutorial explains how the coordinates of the ROC curve are
              obtained from the risk distributions of diseased and non-diseased
