               her belief that the line is in the center. However, after 5
               throws which each land to the left of the line, she may alter her
               belief and move the line toward the right. After another string
               of “lefts,” she may movewhere she thinks the line is even further
               right. Two tosses that land on the right side may cause her to
               reconsider her last change, and she would shift her hypothesis
               leftward a bit. Notice the important way that the Bayesian
               differs from the frequentist – to the Bayesian, the hypothesis is
               changed in the light of new information. We can write this as:",
