              examining feasibility when adapting an intervention tested in
              mainstream populations to a new more diverse group. In Section 2,
              statistical and design issues are presented, including sample
              sizes for pilot studies, estimates of minimally important
              differences, design effects, confidence intervals (CI) and
              nonparametric statistics. An in-depth treatment of the limits of
              effect size estimation as well as process variables is presented.
              Tables showing CI around parameters are provided. With small
              samples, effect size, completion and adherence rate estimates will
              have large CI. CONCLUSION: This commentary offers examples of
              indicators for evaluating feasibility, and of the limits of effect
