  abstract  = "This article presents an overview of fundamental statistical
               principles of clinical trials of pain treatments. Statistical
               considerations relevant to phase 2 proof of concept and phase 3
               confirmatory randomized trials investigating efficacy and safety
               are discussed, including (1) research design; (2) endpoints and
               analyses; (3) sample size determination and statistical power;
               (4) missing data and trial estimands; (5) data monitoring and
