               natural experimental evaluation. Natural experiments therefore
               generate valuable opportunities for evaluating population health,
               health systems, and other interventions, including those that
               are, for practical or ethical reasons, not suitable for
               investigation using randomised controlled trials. One example of
               a natural experiment is the introduction by the Scottish
               government in 2018 of a minimum price at which a unit of alcohol
