              original GRIPP (Guidance for Reporting Involvement of Patients and
              the Public) checklist was revised, based on updated systematic
              review evidence. A three round Delphi survey was used to develop
              consensus on items to be included in the guideline. A subsequent
              face-to-face meeting produced agreement on items not reaching
              consensus during the Delphi process.Results 143 participants
              agreed to participate in round one, with an 86\% (123/143)
              response for round two and a 78\% (112/143) response for round
              three. The Delphi survey identified the need for long form (LF)
