  volume   =  38,
  number   =  7,
  pages    = "778--788",
  abstract = "OBJECTIVES: General frameworks for conducting and reporting health
              economic evaluations are available but not specific enough to
              cover the intricacies of the evaluation of diagnostic tests and
              biomarkers. Such evaluations are typically complex and model-based
              because tests primarily affect health outcomes indirectly and
