               often the result of uncontrolled confounding. Here, we aim to
               provide an overview to causal inference for survival outcomes
               with time-varying exposures for static interventions using
               inverse probability weighting. The basic concepts described here
               can also apply to other types of exposure strategies, although
               these may require additional design or analytic considerations.
