              ``yes'' answers (low risk of bias) on the risk of bias tool.
              CONCLUSION: There is a plethora of published checklists that may
              overwhelm authors looking to efficiently guard against publishing
              in predatory journals. The continued development of such
              checklists may be confusing and of limited benefit. The similarity
