              manuscripts was 6.0 out of 12 possible points (SD 2.6, range
              1-12). Corrected item-total correlations ranged from 0.33 (item 3)
              to 0.58 (item 6), and Cronbach's alpha was 0.68 (internal
              consistency). The intra-class correlation coefficient (average
              measure) was 0.77 [95\% CI 0.57, 0.88] (inter-rater reliability).
              Raters often disagreed on items 1 and 4. Conclusions: SANRA's
              feasibility, inter-rater reliability, homogeneity of items, and
