  volume    =  107,
  number    =  44,
  pages     = "776--782",
  abstract  = "BACKGROUND: Regression analysis is an important statistical
               method for the analysis of medical data. It enables the
               identification and characterization of relationships among
               multiple factors. It also enables the identification of
               prognostically relevant risk factors and the calculation of risk
               scores for individual prognostication. METHODS: This article is
               based on selected textbooks of statistics, a selective review of
