  publisher = "American College of Physicians",
  volume    =  178,
  number    =  8,
  pages     = "1183--1186",
  abstract  = "In 2017, the GRADE (Grading of Recommendations Assessment,
               Development and Evaluation) working group defined the certainty
               of evidence as the certainty that the true effect lies on one
               side of a threshold or in a particular range. This definition has
               proved useful as the basis for rating certainty, facilitating the
               interpretation of the results for the target audience. However,
