              and Berliner, Elise and Trivedi, Madhukar H",
  journal  = "Ann. Intern. Med.",
  volume   =  172,
  number   =  12,
  pages    = "803--809",
  abstract = "Major depressive disorder is a common mental health condition that
              affects an estimated 16.2 million adults and 3.1 million
              adolescents in the United States. Yet, a lack of uniformity
              remains in measurements and monitoring for depression both in
              clinical practice and in research settings. This project aimed to
              develop a minimum set of standardized outcome measures relevant to
              both patients and clinicians that can be collected in depression
              registries and clinical practice. Twenty-nine depression
              registries and related data collection efforts were identified and
              invited to submit outcome measures. Additional measures were
